TICKET-102: Auth — verify Google ID tokens

Priority: P0 · Estimate: 3 pts · Depends on: 101
Every API request must carry a Google ID token from the Android app. Backend verifies signature, audience, and expiry; maps to an internal user record in Firestore.

Tasks

- Middleware verifying ID tokens against Google certs (cached JWKS)
- Firestore `users` collection: `{uid, email, createdAt, locale, refreshTokenRef}`
- Store Gmail OAuth refresh tokens in Secret Manager or KMS-encrypted Firestore field — never plaintext
- Rate limiting per user (e.g., 60 req/min) to protect the Claude API budget

Acceptance criteria

- Requests without valid tokens → 401 with no detail leakage
- Refresh tokens encrypted at rest; key rotation documented
- Unit tests cover expired/wrong-audience/malformed tokens
